{
  "step_1": "The decision reason considers whether a lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., a 100% probability outcome) and prefers the lottery with such a sure outcome. In the decision problem, Lottery A has three outcomes with probabilities 33%, 66%, and 1%, so no outcome is certain. Lottery B yields 2400 Euros with 100% probability, so it has a sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied and would prefer Lottery B because it is the only one with a sure outcome.",
  "step_2": "The individual's verbal report indicates that their initial reaction was concern about the 1% chance of getting nothing in Lottery A. Upon further reflection, they noted that the potential gain of 100 Euros (2500 vs. 2400) in Lottery A occurs only with a 33% chance and comes with the risk of getting nothing. They ultimately chose Lottery B because the potential extra gain does not justify the risk of leaving empty-handed. The individual emphasizes the risk of getting nothing and the certainty of 2400 Euros in Lottery B, highlighting the attractiveness of the guaranteed outcome. The justification centers on risk aversion and the disutility of the 1% chance of zero, but also clearly values the security of a guaranteed amount.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on the presence of a sure outcome and prefers the lottery that provides it. The individual in the verbal report explicitly values the certainty of receiving 2400 Euros in Lottery B and contrasts it with the uncertainty and risk (especially the 1% chance of nothing) in Lottery A. Although the individual also considers the magnitude of potential gains and risk trade-offs, the justification strongly emphasizes the appeal of the guaranteed outcome. This aligns closely with the core logic of the decision reason, even if additional considerations (like risk aversion and utility of gains) are present. The presence of a sure outcome is clearly a central and decisive factor in the individual’s reasoning. Therefore, the decision reason was used, though possibly in conjunction with other considerations.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

{
